{"1-7":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":4,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"javan-h3120g","name":"Javan","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Japheth","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"places":[{"id":"iconium-g2430","name":"Iconium","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"derbe-g1190","name":"Derbe","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"lycaonia-g3071","name":"Lycaonia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"lystra-g3082","name":"Lystra","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":6}],"words":[{"base":"G2453","lemma":"Ἰουδαῖος","tr":"Ioudaios","gloss":"Jew","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":194},{"base":"G4862","lemma":"σύν","tr":"sun","gloss":"with","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":128},{"base":"G4128","lemma":"πλῆθος","tr":"plēthos","gloss":"multitude","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":31},{"base":"G1096","lemma":"γίνομαι","tr":"ginomai","gloss":"to be","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":668},{"base":"G1484","lemma":"ἔθνος","tr":"ethnos","gloss":"Gentiles","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":162},{"base":"G4172","lemma":"πόλις","tr":"polis","gloss":"city","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":163},{"base":"G3303","lemma":"μέν","tr":"men","gloss":"on the other hand","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":178},{"base":"G5037","lemma":"τε","tr":"te","gloss":"and","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":215},{"base":"G1892","lemma":"ἐπεγείρω","tr":"epegeirō","gloss":"to awaken","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G2703","lemma":"καταφεύγω","tr":"katapheugō","gloss":"to flee","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"HEB","chapter":2,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"and was affirmed by God through signs, wonders, various miracles, and gifts of the Holy Spirit distributed according to His will.","from":3},{"book":"ACT","chapter":13,"verse":50,"verseEnd":50,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"The Jews, however, incited the religious women of prominence and the leading men of the city. They stirred up persecution against Paul and Barnabas and drove them out of their district.","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":13,"verse":45,"verseEnd":45,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"But when the Jews saw the crowds, they were filled with jealousy, and they blasphemously contradicted what Paul was saying.","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":14,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Then some Jews arrived from Antioch and Iconium and won over the crowds. They stoned Paul and dragged him outside the city, presuming he was dead.","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":17,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The Jews, however, became jealous. So they brought in some troublemakers from the marketplace, formed a mob, and sent the city into an uproar. They raided Jasonʼs house in search of Paul and Silas, hoping to bring them out to the people.","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":21,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"When the seven days were almost over, some Jews from the province of Asia saw Paul at the temple. They stirred up the whole crowd and seized him,","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":21,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"The whole city was stirred up, and the people rushed together. They seized Paul and dragged him out of the temple, and at once the gates were shut.","from":2},{"book":"EPH","chapter":6,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"Pray in the Spirit at all times, with every kind of prayer and petition. To this end, stay alert with all perseverance in your prayers for all the saints.","from":3}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"8-18":{"people":[{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":4,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"barnabas-g0921g","name":"Barnabas","kind":"person","brief":"Brother of Mary","count":2,"firstVerse":12}],"places":[{"id":"lystra-g3082","name":"Lystra","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"lycaonia-g3071","name":"Lycaonia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11}],"words":[{"base":"G3972","lemma":"Παῦλος","tr":"Paulos","gloss":"Paul","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":158},{"base":"G3793","lemma":"ὄχλος","tr":"ochlos","gloss":"crowd","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":175},{"base":"G2203","lemma":"Ζεύς, Δίς","tr":"Zeus, Dis","gloss":"Zeus","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":2},{"base":"G5037","lemma":"τε","tr":"te","gloss":"and","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":215},{"base":"G2380","lemma":"θύω","tr":"thuō","gloss":"to sacrifice","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":14},{"base":"G0921","lemma":"Βαρνάβας","tr":"Barnabas","gloss":"Barnabas","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":28},{"base":"G4160","lemma":"ποιέω","tr":"poieō","gloss":"to do","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":569},{"base":"G4228","lemma":"πούς","tr":"pous","gloss":"foot","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":93},{"base":"G4043","lemma":"περιπατέω","tr":"peripateō","gloss":"to walk","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":94},{"base":"G1909","lemma":"ἐπί","tr":"epi","gloss":"upon","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":885}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ACT","chapter":17,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Although God overlooked the ignorance of earlier times, He now commands all people everywhere to repent.","from":16},{"book":"ROM","chapter":1,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"For what may be known about God is plain to them, because God has made it plain to them.","from":17},{"book":"ROM","chapter":1,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"For since the creation of the world Godʼs invisible qualities, His eternal power and divine nature, have been clearly seen, being understood from His workmanship, so that men are without excuse.","from":17},{"book":"ACT","chapter":10,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"But Peter helped him up. “Stand up,” he said, “I am only a man myself.”","from":15},{"book":"1CO","chapter":8,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":8,"source":"openbible","text":"So about eating food sacrificed to idols: We know that an idol is nothing at all in the world, and that there is no God but one.","from":15},{"book":"JAS","chapter":5,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Elijah was a man just like us. He prayed earnestly that it would not rain, and it did not rain on the land for three and a half years.","from":15},{"book":"1SA","chapter":12,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Do not turn aside after worthless things that cannot profit you or deliver you, for they are empty.","from":15},{"book":"JOB","chapter":5,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"He gives rain to the earth and sends water upon the fields.","from":17}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":3},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2}]},"19-23":{"people":[{"id":"judah-h3063g","name":"Judah","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"paul-g3972g","name":"Paul","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"barnabas-g0921g","name":"Barnabas","kind":"person","brief":"Brother of Mary","count":1,"firstVerse":20}],"places":[{"id":"antioch-g0490h","name":"Antioch","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"iconium-g2430","name":"Iconium","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"derbe-g1190","name":"Derbe","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"lystra-g3082","name":"Lystra","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"words":[{"base":"G2430","lemma":"Ἰκόνιον","tr":"Ikonion","gloss":"Iconium","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"G4172","lemma":"πόλις","tr":"polis","gloss":"city","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":163},{"base":"G0490","lemma":"Ἀντιόχεια","tr":"Antiocheia","gloss":"Antioch","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":18},{"base":"G1525","lemma":"εἰσέρχομαι","tr":"eiserchomai","gloss":"to enter","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":194},{"base":"G3101","lemma":"μαθητής","tr":"mathētēs","gloss":"disciple","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":261},{"base":"G5500","lemma":"χειροτονέω","tr":"cheirotoneō","gloss":"to appoint","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G1191","lemma":"Δέρβη","tr":"Derbē","gloss":"Derbe","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G1696","lemma":"ἐμμένω","tr":"emmenō","gloss":"to abide in","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G1991","lemma":"ἐπιστηρίζω","tr":"epistērizō","gloss":"to strengthen","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G2944","lemma":"κυκλόω","tr":"kukloō","gloss":"to surround","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1PE","chapter":5,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":38,"source":"both","text":"And after you have suffered for a little while, the God of all grace, who has called you to His eternal glory in Christ, will Himself restore you, secure you, strengthen you, and establish you.","from":22},{"book":"2TI","chapter":3,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":36,"source":"both","text":"Indeed, all who desire to live godly lives in Christ Jesus will be persecuted,","from":22},{"book":"JHN","chapter":16,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":32,"source":"both","text":"I have told you these things so that in Me you may have peace. In the world you will have tribulation. But take courage; I have overcome the world!”","from":22},{"book":"1TH","chapter":3,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"We sent Timothy, our brother and fellow worker for God in the gospel of Christ, to strengthen and encourage you in your faith,","from":22},{"book":"1TH","chapter":3,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":19,"source":"both","text":"Indeed, when we were with you, we kept warning you that we would suffer persecution; and as you know, it has come to pass.","from":22},{"book":"ROM","chapter":8,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"And if we are children, then we are heirs: heirs of God and co-heirs with Christ—if indeed we suffer with Him, so that we may also be glorified with Him.","from":22},{"book":"REV","chapter":2,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"Do not fear what you are about to suffer. Behold, the devil is about to throw some of you into prison to test you, and you will suffer tribulation for ten days. Be faithful even unto death, and I will give you the crown of life.","from":22},{"book":"2CO","chapter":11,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Three times I was beaten with rods, once I was stoned, three times I was shipwrecked. I spent a night and a day in the open sea.","from":19}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":3},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2}]},"24-28":{"people":[],"places":[{"id":"pamphylia-g3828","name":"Pamphylia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"pisidia-g4099","name":"Pisidia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"attalia-g0825","name":"Attalia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"perga-g4011","name":"Perga","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"antioch-g0490g","name":"Antioch","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":26}],"words":[{"base":"G4099","lemma":"Πισιδία","tr":"Pisidia","gloss":"Pisidia","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G4011","lemma":"Πέργη","tr":"Pergē","gloss":"Perga","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G0636","lemma":"ἀποπλέω","tr":"apopleō","gloss":"to set sail","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G3828","lemma":"Παμφυλία","tr":"Pamphulia","gloss":"Pamphylia","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"G1304","lemma":"διατρίβω","tr":"diatribō","gloss":"to remain","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"G0312","lemma":"ἀναγγέλλω","tr":"anangellō","gloss":"to report","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"G3606","lemma":"ὅθεν","tr":"hothen","gloss":"whence","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":15},{"base":"G0490","lemma":"Ἀντιόχεια","tr":"Antiocheia","gloss":"Antioch","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"G3854","lemma":"παραγίνομαι","tr":"paraginomai","gloss":"to come","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":36},{"base":"G2374","lemma":"θύρα","tr":"thura","gloss":"door","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":39}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1CO","chapter":16,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"because a great door for effective work has opened to me, even though many oppose me.","from":27},{"book":"ACT","chapter":15,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"The whole assembly fell silent as they listened to Barnabas and Paul describing the signs and wonders God had done among the Gentiles through them.","from":27},{"book":"2CO","chapter":2,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Now when I went to Troas to preach the gospel of Christ and a door stood open for me in the Lord,","from":27},{"book":"COL","chapter":4,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"as you pray also for us, that God may open to us a door for the word, so that we may proclaim the mystery of Christ, for which I am in chains.","from":27},{"book":"ACT","chapter":15,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"but Paul chose Silas and left, commended by the brothers to the grace of the Lord.","from":26},{"book":"1CO","chapter":5,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When you are assembled in the name of our Lord Jesus and I am with you in spirit, along with the power of the Lord Jesus,","from":27},{"book":"JHN","chapter":9,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"“How then were your eyes opened?” they asked.","from":27},{"book":"ACT","chapter":11,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"When they heard this, they had not further objections, and they glorified God, saying, “So then, God has granted even the Gentiles repentance unto life.”","from":27}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}